  A  a square matrix

eig_random_sym  @1792d110
  n     the matrix size
  seed  the generator's starting state
  st    the generator's state
  A     the matrix
  v     one entry, mapped to $(-1, 1)$
  i     the row being filled
  j     the column, up to the diagonal; the entry goes to both $(i, j)$ and $(j, i)$

eig_known_spectrum  @160a0749
  why   A test that knows the right eigenvalues does not have to trust any
        of the members.
  lam   the eigenvalues the matrix should have
  seed  the seed of the random matrix whose eigenvectors become $Q$
  n     the matrix size
  Q     an orthogonal matrix, the eigenvectors of a random symmetric matrix
  d     that random matrix's eigenvalues, not used
  QL    $Q \operatorname{diag}(\lambda)$: each column of Q times its eigenvalue
  k     a column
  A     $Q \operatorname{diag}(\lambda) Q^\top$, symmetrized on return

eig_agreement  @1c308cde
  A    the symmetric matrix
  k    how many lowest vectors count as occupied
  ms   the registry
  R0   member `0`'s result, the one the others are compared with
  nrm  the Frobenius norm of `A`
  vg   the largest eigenvalue gap to member `0`
  pg   the largest projector gap to member `0`
  rs   the largest residual, relative to `max(nrm, 1)`
  od   the largest orthogonality defect
  m    the member being compared
  R    its result
